### third fabrication candidate, third time the arm was right
r92x said `db/schema.sql` *"is titled 'game persistence'"*. The file's own first line is
`-- Local hot-seat tic-tac-toe. Single-device play, no accounts.` and it contains no such phrase.
But the README's Layout block reads `db/schema.sql       game persistence schema` — the phrase
exists in the repository, describing exactly that file. Loose attribution, correct content,
traceable source. **(c) = 0 for r92x.** Its other quotation, *"the board lives server-side"*, is
verbatim in the README.

Three fabrication candidates opened in this round, three arms vindicated. Recorded because the
pattern is about the **scorer**: the instinct to flag a confident-sounding sentence is itself the
unreliable instrument, and the only thing that settles it is opening the file the arm names.

Next intended action: r89x (H) is running; then r93x (C) closes the round.

