## the finding that outranks the round
r93x also wrote that the parent project's `AGENTS.md` governs that project and not its directory.
**It never opened that file.** `grep` over the three control transcripts: all three mention
`AGENTS.md`, **none has a tool call on it**, and the raw JSONL shows it injected as
`"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":".../bemyagent/AGENTS.md","type":"Project",
"content":"Read .bemyagent/docs/00-ai-rules.md before every task."}` together with the session's
`MEMORY.md`, under *"IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior."*

So the control condition has never been what it was labelled, in any round. Written up in
`harness/README.md` with the direction of the bias: benefit readings understated, harm readings
inflated. Not fixable from inside this session.

